{"sourceSha256": "18f1de02e2d8505a349773d7e039e3ff80c960f6216181a822993d732caffe50", "text": "Dear Dr Smiley,\nRe: Elizabeth Miro, DOB 23/10/70\n\nThank you for seeing Mrs Miro, a 48-year-old mother of three young children who has been\ndiagnosed with inflammatory breast cancer and requires urgent assessment and\n\nmanagement.\n\nMrs Miro initially presented one month ago with a three-week history of nght breast pain\n\nalong with swelling warmth and redness. On examination, her breast was enlarged, tender\nand exhibited signs of periareolar erythema with non-tender multiple axillary lymph nodes.\nThere were no nipple discharge or retraction. Therefore, flucloxacillin was prescribed and\nultrasound and mammogram were ordered.\n\nMrs Miro defaulted her subsequent appointments. and on yesterday’s consultation reported\nno improvement in her symptoms despite having completed a course of antibiotics. Her\nbreast was tender and swollen with pitted skin (peau d orange) and nipple retraction.\nImaging findings revealed malignant changes in her right breast. She underwent a core-\nneedle biopsy and the results today show infiltrating ductal carcinoma. | have ordered a full\nblood count and requested that the results be sent to you.\n\nShe has a strong family history of cancer in her mother (ovarian cancer, age 69) and her\nmatemal aunt (diec of breast cancer, age 73). She was diagnosed with depression in 2015\n\nand is currently experiencing significant symptoms of depression for which she was referred\n\nto a psychiatrist and fluoxetine was prescnbed.\n\nPlease do not hesitate to contact me if you require further information.\n\nYours sincerely,\nDr. X", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "Dear Dr Smiley,\nRe: Elizabeth Miro, DOB 23/10/70\n\nThank you for seeing Mrs Miro, a 48-year-old mother of three young children who has been\ndiagnosed with inflammatory breast cancer and requires urgent assessment and\n\nmanagement.\n\nMrs Miro initially presented one month ago with a three-week history of nght breast pain\n\nalong with swelling warmth and redness. On examination, her breast was enlarged, tender\nand exhibited signs of periareolar erythema with non-tender multiple axillary lymph nodes.\nThere were no nipple discharge or retraction. Therefore, flucloxacillin was prescribed and\nultrasound and mammogram were ordered.\n\nMrs Miro defaulted her subsequent appointments. and on yesterday’s consultation reported\nno improvement in her symptoms despite having completed a course of antibiotics. Her\nbreast was tender and swollen with pitted skin (peau d orange) and nipple retraction.\nImaging findings revealed malignant changes in her right breast. She underwent a core-\nneedle biopsy and the results today show infiltrating ductal carcinoma. | have ordered a full\nblood count and requested that the results be sent to you.\n\nShe has a strong family history of cancer in her mother (ovarian cancer, age 69) and her\nmatemal aunt (diec of breast cancer, age 73). She was diagnosed with depression in 2015\n\nand is currently experiencing significant symptoms of depression for which she was referred\n\nto a psychiatrist and fluoxetine was prescnbed.\n\nPlease do not hesitate to contact me if you require further information.\n\nYours sincerely,\nDr. X", "extraction": "ocr", "layout": {"version": 1, "width": 2217.0, "height": 2800.0, "blocks": [{"text": "Dear Dr Smiley,\nRe: Elizabeth Miro, DOB 23/10/70", "lines": [{"text": "Dear Dr Smiley,", "x": 0.01128, "y": 0.01143, "width": 0.15787, "height": 0.01714, "confidence": 0.901, "words": [{"text": "Dear", "x": 0.01128, "width": 0.04917, "confidence": 0.964}, {"text": "Dr", "x": 0.06676, "width": 0.02436, "confidence": 0.886}, {"text": "Smiley,", "x": 0.09608, "width": 0.07307, "confidence": 0.854}], "uncertainWords": []}, {"text": "Re: Elizabeth Miro, DOB 23/10/70", "x": 0.01128, "y": 0.05143, "width": 0.35498, "height": 0.0175, "confidence": 0.953, "words": [{"text": "Re:", "x": 0.01128, "width": 0.03